```java
/**
 * Desktop startup (chapter 18 §1): issues this Host's one-use launch URI and hands it to the platform
 * browser. The URI carries no token — the launch secret stays in the channel — so nothing secret can
 * reach browser history or process output.
 *
 * @return false when no platform browser accepted the URI
 */
public boolean openPwaInBrowser(BrowserLauncher browser) {
    return browser.open(launchUri());
}
```

Where to put `BrowserLauncher`? host-web (next to LocalBrowserLaunch) — it's a web/desktop concern. And `LocalHostApplication` (ji-cli) imports it. ji-cli depends on ji-host-web. ✓

